From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akramboussanni <92455979+akramboussanni@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:22:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] gnome: Take prayer times from Kimono instead of Mawaqit and
 AlAdhan
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Why: Kimono Prayer already looks up Mawaqit, MasjidBox and calculated times on
the server and remembers each person's place across their devices. The
extension should show exactly that, not scrape mawaqit.net or call AlAdhan.

What must survive upstream changes:
- extension.js's _request is the only thing that goes online, always through
  state.link:
    GET <link>                        -> { place, timetable, recent, problem? }
    GET <link>?q=<text>               -> { places }  (words, a mosque link, "lat, lon")
    GET <link>?lat=&lon=&tz=<IANA>    -> { places }  (the location button; tz is the local zone)
    PUT <link> {"id"}                 -> same as GET (choosing a result)
  Non-200 answers carry { error }, shown as the status. 401 means the link was
  renewed: the link is forgotten (times kept) and the status says to connect
  again from Kimono Prayer.
- No mawaqit.net, AlAdhan or other source URL is left: calendar.js loses the
  Mawaqit page parser, slug parser and AlAdhan parser, and extension.js loses
  the "Use calculated prayer times" submenu and suggestion (calculated places
  come back as search results).
- kimono.js calendarFromTimetable() turns timetable.days into upstream's
  yearly calendar (calendar[month - 1]['<day>'] = the six times). schedule(),
  the highlighting, night milestones, countdown title and notifications are
  upstream's, unchanged. The once-a-year refresh gate is dropped: the feed spans
  the new year by itself.
- state.place is Kimono's place (id, kind, name, detail, url). The menu names
  it, and the source line always reads "Kimono · Mawaqit" / "MasjidBox" /
  "Calculated" with the place's detail (the calculation method for calculated
  times, plus the may-differ note).
- It refreshes on enable, then hourly while connected (so a place chosen on
  another device shows up), and on Refresh.
- tests/kimono.mjs (node) covers the conversion; tests/calendar.js (gjs)
  schedules a New Year from it.

